1
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:45,040
Well, well.

2
00:00:46,040 --> 00:00:47,960
The shop is getting famous now, huh?

3
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:50,200
With so many people sharing

4
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:52,720
You must be making a lot of money by scamming.

5
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:54,400
Nammon.

6
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:57,240
Saw the post last night and laughed so hard.

7
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,520
What was it? Love Lab shop offering all kinds of services?

8
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:03,600
Sounds really good.

9
00:01:03,880 --> 00:01:06,880
But why aren't the people here good at all?

10
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:11,000
If you're just here to be sarcastic,

11
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:13,320
just say it and leave.

12
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:26,760
Oh, is this her?

13
00:01:26,760 --> 00:01:28,920
Claire's new customer?

14
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:34,040
You should be careful.

15
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:37,280
Claire is great at making people fall in love.

16
00:01:37,680 --> 00:01:39,800
She's great at taking care of people.

17
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:42,440
But honestly, it's all just an act.

18
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:44,840
Stop crossing the line, Nammon.

19
00:01:45,760 --> 00:01:47,960
You don't even know her.

20
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:50,000
Stop making up nonsense here.

21
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:52,920
Why does that matter?

22
00:01:52,920 --> 00:01:54,960
I don't even need to know this woman.

23
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:57,120
But I know your true nature very well.

24
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:58,120
That's enough.

25
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:00,240
I don't know why you're here.

26
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:02,320
Our story ended a long time ago.

27
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:04,600
Claire owes you nothing anymore.

28
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:08,680
I came because I want to know...

29
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:12,120
if Claire is still good at faking and making excuses.

30
00:02:13,160 --> 00:02:14,160
Hey, you.

31
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:16,440
If you plan on getting serious with her,

32
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:17,840
I'm warning you.

33
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:21,800
Once she gets what she wants,

34
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:23,400
she'll throw you away like trash.

35
00:02:24,320 --> 00:02:26,960
Pretending to open a shop for hire,

36
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:28,960
helping this person and that person.

37
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:32,840
But the truth is, she's just a fake, greedy.

38
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:38,120
Who's the real fake here?

39
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:49,320
There are no secrets in this world.

40
00:02:51,040 --> 00:02:52,000
Just you wait.

41
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:23,600
Claire.

42
00:03:27,440 --> 00:03:28,400
You should go back.

43
00:03:30,280 --> 00:03:31,880
Don't stay near someone like me.

44
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:41,600
I don't deserve anyone's love.

45
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:55,920
Eris doesn't know what you has been through.

46
00:03:56,360 --> 00:03:57,080
What I'm certain of is that

47
00:03:57,080 --> 00:03:58,840
the person in front of me right now

48
00:03:58,840 --> 00:04:00,520
is not a bad person.

49
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:02,680
You're not a terrible person.

50
00:04:03,560 --> 00:04:04,800
I can feel it.

51
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:09,440
Care is strong, always protecting others.

52
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:13,720
If you ever feel like there's no one left,

53
00:04:13,720 --> 00:04:15,160
I'm still right here.

54
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:25,680
The past cannot be changed.

55
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:30,160
But we can make today and the future better.

56
00:04:31,040 --> 00:04:33,800
I might not completely understand it all.

57
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:36,480
But I'm ready to learn and understand you

58
00:04:36,480 --> 00:04:37,720
just the way you are.

59
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:47,800
Thank you, Eris.

60
00:05:07,520 --> 00:05:09,640
I have never told my own story

61
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:12,400
to any customer since starting this job.

62
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:14,960
And what about now?

63
00:05:16,320 --> 00:05:17,120
Can you tell me?

64
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:19,520
Yeah.

65
00:05:21,480 --> 00:05:22,800
When I was young,

66
00:05:23,960 --> 00:05:25,440
I hated love.

67
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:29,680
Because I saw Mom cry almost every day.

68
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:33,440
After Dad left us.

69
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:36,520
Mom once told me that,

70
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:39,440
if it weren't for me,

71
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:44,160
Mom wouldn't want to live anymore.

72
00:05:46,560 --> 00:05:48,160
Ever since then,

73
00:05:48,960 --> 00:05:52,600
I never believed love could truly make anyone happy.

74
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:57,120
It only brings people suffering.

75
00:05:58,480 --> 00:06:00,040
Makes people sad.

76
00:06:02,080 --> 00:06:06,480
So I built up very high walls.

77
00:06:08,880 --> 00:06:10,960
Afraid to love anyone.

78
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:14,800
Afraid to even form an attachment to anyone.

79
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:18,640
Because of the fear that in the end,

80
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:22,080
I would have to lose them too.

81
00:06:24,840 --> 00:06:25,720
And what about now?

82
00:06:29,920 --> 00:06:33,680
I just feel that when I'm with you,

83
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:37,920
I doesn't have to be strong all the time.

84
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:45,280
It's comforting and feels very safe.

85
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:50,280
I feel the same way.

86
00:07:09,760 --> 00:07:10,880
I thinks...

87
00:07:13,200 --> 00:07:14,640
I'm starting to fall for you.

88
00:07:21,680 --> 00:07:23,000
I like you too.

89
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:36,640
Eris...

90
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:53,080
I think...

91
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:56,640
I can't hold it anymore.

92
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:13,320
My stomach hurts.

93
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:15,800
The Som Tum from noon must be acting up.

94
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:16,880
Can I use the restroom?

95
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:19,640
Okay, okay.

96
00:08:35,840 --> 00:08:37,040
Help me!

97
00:08:42,040 --> 00:08:42,920
Careful, it's slippery.

98
00:08:59,040 --> 00:08:59,840
I'm sorry.

99
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:12,120
Someone is hungry.

100
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:14,160
Want to eat something? I will cook it for you.

101
00:09:15,520 --> 00:09:17,160
With diarrhea like this, it has to be rice porridge.

102
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:18,560
Sound good?

103
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:21,000
Yeah.

104
00:09:21,680 --> 00:09:22,480
Okay.

105
00:09:34,600 --> 00:09:36,520
Well, let me help.

106
00:09:54,240 --> 00:09:58,920
Uh, Claire, I'd better do it alone.

107
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:04,000
Then let me...

108
00:10:06,080 --> 00:10:07,280
take care of the porridge.

109
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:11,600
It's hot!

110
00:10:12,120 --> 00:10:13,120
Are you okay?

111
00:10:18,960 --> 00:10:20,760
Go sit and wait over there.

112
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:24,520
I'll serve you once it's done.

113
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:27,960
Alright.

114
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:16,320
Sleeping like a baby.

115
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:22,480
You doesn't need to act strong all the time.

116
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:31,320
I'm sorry.

117
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:32,120
I accidentally fell asleep.

118
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:33,720
What time is it?

119
00:11:34,560 --> 00:11:36,000
It's past 9 PM.

120
00:11:36,520 --> 00:11:37,680
9 PM already?

121
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:40,000
It's really late.

122
00:11:40,520 --> 00:11:42,640
I'll head back so you can rest.

123
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:44,120
It's okay.

124
00:11:45,040 --> 00:11:47,160
Going back late is dangerous.

125
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,800
You can sleep here tonight.

126
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:53,000
Is that okay?

127
00:11:56,240 --> 00:11:57,160
It's fine.

128
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:59,960
So I won't have to worry about you.

129
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:06,360
Alright then.

130
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:11,120
Here's the rice porridge I made for you.

131
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:16,080
Looks delicious.

132
00:12:27,360 --> 00:12:28,160
How is it?

133
00:12:29,240 --> 00:12:30,040
Is it good?

134
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:32,080
Very delicious.

135
00:13:45,360 --> 00:13:47,800
I think you can wear this.

136
00:13:51,640 --> 00:13:52,560
Thank you.

137
00:13:54,920 --> 00:13:57,600
The bathroom is downstairs here.

138
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:16,480
Keep it together, Claire.

139
00:14:17,760 --> 00:14:19,200
I'm so tense right now.

140
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:48,120
Eris.

141
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:50,880
Where can I put this?

142
00:14:52,840 --> 00:14:54,680
Come, I will put it away.

143
00:14:57,120 --> 00:14:59,560
It's okay, I can do it myself.

144
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:03,440
Then you can put it over there.

145
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:26,400
Are you asleep?

146
00:15:30,240 --> 00:15:31,040
Not yet.

147
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,000
Can't sleep?

148
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:38,240
Are you uncomfortable?

149
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:41,000
I will check the pillow for you.

150
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:38,480
Your hands are so cold.

151
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:42,920
The AC is cold.

152
00:17:04,120 --> 00:17:05,240
Then do you want to move closer?

153
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:26,800
Is it warmer?

154
00:17:28,600 --> 00:17:29,400
Yeah.

155
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:26,440
Every time I see you right in front of me,

156
00:18:26,440 --> 00:18:29,200
My heart tells me to hide my feelings first.
